    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The exposé should focus on a few specific, well-defined research questions, and describe experiments that tackle these questions in great detail. The research question and subquestions are stated but are formulated as very broad and general questions. Subsequently, the approach chapter does not contain a detailed enough description of the experimental setup. The exposé would improve a lot by narrowing the focus and giving more details about the planned implementation.."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet",
      "indent": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Theoretical Framework",
